# MEASURED DEFECT, pinned here so it cannot recur on checkout.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on this host converts LF to CRLF when git touches a
# text file. That bit the evidence sidecars once already: a sidecar written
# as "<sha>  name.json\n" was read as "<sha>  name.json\r", and
# `sha256sum -c` failed with `FAILED open or read` because the trailing CR
# became part of the FILENAME.
#
# A sidecar is machine-read, not human-read. It must keep LF on every host,
# or the only reproducible receipt identity in the repository stops working.
# eol=lf stores LF in the blob and checks out LF regardless of platform.
receipts/*.sha256 text eol=lf

# The register is deliberately CRLF in the worktree and in the blob. Pinning
# it stops a checkout on another host from silently flipping 2145 lines to LF
# and invalidating the line-ending clause recorded in Phase 9/10.
docs/EVIDENCE_REGISTER.md text eol=crlf
docs/report.html text eol=crlf
